Paper restructure to top-venue conventions: findings-first main text (claim-titled results paragraphs, experiment names instead of codes, one registration sentence plus the interaction-sign footnote, registered-prediction counts from fig_registered), appendix by topic (related work, benchmark, systems, prompts, settings, registered analysis plan, extended results, error analysis, limitations, datasheet) with a contents list; version table, readings table, deviation table and decision-log references leave the paper

Generators drop ID prefixes and provenance from captions; registered_counts.tex is generated; tab_round3 splits into tab_refresh_upsert and tab_natural. Generated numbers are refreshed after the final restaging of the re-run analyses.

